Compile-time and container-runtime dependency jars for Gumdrop.

**Not in git.** Only this README is tracked; `lib/*.jar` is gitignored. A fresh
clone needs network access once for `ant resolve-deps` (invoked automatically
from compile and `assemble-container` targets).

Version pins: `boms/versions.properties` (keep in sync with root `pom.xml` and
`central/*-pom.xml` when cutting releases).

## Downloaded by `ant resolve-deps`

| Jar | Source |
|-----|--------|
| gonzalez-core-* | Maven Central (`org.bluezoo:gonzalez-core`) |
| jsonparser-* | Maven Central (`org.bluezoo:jsonparser`) |
| jprotobuf-* | Maven Central (`org.bluezoo:jprotobuf`) |
| jakarta.servlet-api-* | Maven Central (Jakarta Servlet 6.x API) |
| jakarta.annotation-api-* | Maven Central (Jakarta Annotations) |
| jakarta.persistence-api-* | Maven Central (Jakarta Persistence; compile classpath) |
| javax.mail-* | Maven Central (JavaMail API) |
| javax.annotation-api-* | Maven Central (legacy J2EE annotations) |
| javax.ejb-api-* | Maven Central (legacy J2EE EJB API) |
| javax.persistence-api-* | Maven Central (legacy JPA API) |
| jaxws-api-* | Maven Central (JAX-WS API) |

Gumdrop 3 servlet code uses **Jakarta** Servlet and related APIs. The **javax.***
jars remain on the container classpath for older webapp/API surface (mail, EJB,
JPA, JAX-WS) used by parts of the stack and sample dependencies.

## Runtime layout

- **Container install (`dist/container-home/lib/`):** third-party and API jars stay
  as plain files; `ContainerClassLoader` loads them at runtime.
- **Legacy fat jar:** the same jars are nested inside `gumdrop-container.jar`
  (deprecated; prefer `assemble-container` / the zip distribution).
